{
  "summary": "Breaks the circular include dependency between node/blockstorage and validation. It moves ImportBlocks into node/chainstate, moves FatalError to kernel/fatal_error.h, encapsulates BlockManager private state accessed by validation with dedicated methods (such as RequestPrune and MarkBlockIndexDirty), and removes the circular dependency entry from the linter.",
  "problem": "node/blockstorage and validation depend on each other's headers, requiring an explicit exception in test/lint/lint-circular-dependencies.py. Additionally, validation previously held friend access to BlockManager to manipulate private pruning flags and dirty block index sets.",
  "evidence": [
    "The PR removes node/blockstorage -> validation -> node/blockstorage from EXPECTED_CIRCULAR_DEPENDENCIES in test/lint/lint-circular-dependencies.py.",
    "The author notes that after dropping friend declarations and introducing RequestPrune and MarkBlockIndexDirty, 'nothing outside BlockManager writes its private state or the block tree database.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36738"
    ],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The PR branch is based on and currently includes commits from #36738, which move block writing and pruning logic into BlockManager and add tests for failed prune flush retries.",
  "changed_since_previous": "The patch now includes base commits from #36738 that move block storage writing and pruning bookkeeping into BlockManager and retain pruned files across failed flushes.",
  "card": "Breaks the circular header dependency between node/blockstorage and validation. Currently, blockstorage includes validation.h for FatalError and cs_main while validation accesses BlockManager private members as a friend, requiring an exemption in circular dependency linting. This change moves ImportBlocks to node/chainstate, relocates FatalError to kernel/fatal_error.h, and replaces friend declarations with dedicated BlockManager methods. This PR depends on #36738.",
